From: ImmortalWrt Developer <developer@immortalwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: hnat: sync MIB accounting to physical, DSA, and virtual interfaces

Currently, when hardware flow offloading (HNAT) is active, traffic statistics
(bytes and packets) are accounted inside the PPE hardware MIB counters. However,
these statistics are not reported to Linux network devices (DSA user ports such
as wan/lan1~lan4, bridge devices such as br-lan/br-wan, and virtual interfaces),
leaving their ifconfig / /proc/net/dev counters near zero while eth0 accumulates
all raw MAC bytes. Furthermore, bandwidth monitoring tools relying on
nf_conntrack accounting (e.g. nlbwmon) receive no accounting updates for offloaded flows.

This patch fixes the issue by:
1. Recording both primary/physical interface and upper/virtual/bridge interface
   indices (iif, oif, iif_vif, oif_vif) upon flow binding in skb_to_hnat_info().
2. Supporting ndo_flow_offload_stats64_add, per-CPU sw netstats (dev->tstats used
   by DSA user ports and bridges), and standard dev->stats in hnat_update_dev_stats().
3. Updating both ingress interface(s) (as RX) and egress interface(s) (as TX)
   with MIB deltas in hnat_vif_acct_update().
4. Adding a periodic background delayed workqueue in hnat.c running every 1s
   to poll MIB deltas from hardware for active bound flows and update both
   interfaces and nf_conntrack.
5. Enabling nf_stat_en by default so nf_conntrack counters are updated for
   monitoring tools such as nlbwmon.
6. Adding spinlock protection around hardware PPE MIB search registers to
   prevent race conditions between background polling and softirq callbacks.

Signed-off-by: ImmortalWrt Developer <developer@immortalwrt.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_hnat/hnat.h
@@ -978,6 +978,8 @@
 	struct nf_conntrack_zone zone;
 	int iif; /* ingress device ifindex */
 	int oif; /* egress device ifindex */
+	int iif_vif; /* ingress virtual/bridge device ifindex */
+	int oif_vif; /* egress virtual/bridge device ifindex */
 };
 
